        public int parseVersion(String versionFromFile) throws Exception {
            String[] parts = versionFromFile.split("\\.");
            if (parts.length != 2 || !parts[0].matches("[0-9]+") || !parts[1].matches("[0-9]+")) {
                throw new Exception("Invalid EPUB version format: " + versionFromFile);
            }
            int major = Integer.parseInt(parts[0]);
            int minor = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]);

            if (major < 2 || major > 12) {
                throw new Exception("Invalid EPUB version major number");
            }

            if (minor < 0 || minor > 5) {
                throw new Exception("Invalid EPUB version minor number");
            }
            return major * 10000 + minor;
        }

    }

}

```

In the code above, we first parse a version string and validate its format. We then check for any invalid versions by trying to parse them as EPUB versions. If an invalid version is found, it throws an exception.

You can use this class like this:

```java
Main main = new Main();
main.validateFile();
```

Note: This code assumes that the EPUB file has a single line with "version" or "layout". If your EPUB file may have multiple lines, you can use a more sophisticated parsing method.
